      "id": "deployment_notes",
      "filename": "deployment-notes.md",
      "mediaType": "text/markdown",
      "content": "# Recall deployment handbook\n\n## Staging\n\nThe staging cluster is named falcon-staging and runs in eu-west-1.\nIt is sized for integration tests and is rebuilt every night from the\nTerraform modules in the platform-infra repository. Staging nodes use\nspot instances and are allowed to restart without notice. Operators reach\nstaging through the bastion in the shared services account; the cluster\nitself is not reachable from the public internet. Logs from staging are\nretained for seven days because the environment is disposable.\n\n## Change process\n\nRollbacks require two approvals from the platform team.\nA normal deployment needs one approval from the service owner and a green\nintegration run. Deployments are frozen during the December code freeze,\nand a weekly change freeze also applies every Friday after 16:00 UTC.\nThe on-call rotation is published every Monday in the handbook calendar.\nEmergency changes may skip the review queue but still need an incident\nlink in the change record. Every change record must name a rollback plan.\n\n## Storage\n\nPostgres backups are kept for thirty days in the archive bucket.\nThe archive bucket is named recall-archive-2026 and lives in the same\nregion as production. Backups are encrypted with the platform KMS key\nand restored monthly during the disaster-recovery drill. Object lifecycle\nrules move backups older than thirty days to cold storage before deletion.\nThe restore drill is scheduled on the first Tuesday of each month.\n\n## Production and incidents\n\nThe production cluster is named falcon-prod and runs in us-east-2.\nProduction nodes are spread across three availability zones and use the\ngraviton instance family. Cluster upgrades follow the blue-green runbook\nand must be announced in the platform-ops channel one day in advance.\nA sev1 incident pages the on-call engineer through Opsgenie immediately.\nThe incident commander opens a shared timeline within ten minutes and\nposts updates every thirty minutes until the incident is resolved.\nA blameless postmortem is due within five business days, and every action\nitem must have an owner and a due date. Customer-facing incidents also\nrequire a status page update.\n"
    }
